From: xxlloydzz <xxlloydzz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topaz-0951: soc_map: wait for the root vnode before polling
 sweet_ufs

Usability fix (xxlloydzz, mentored by Ma) for a unit-specific modem=1
boot wedge. On this topaz unit (4 GB / 128 GB) every modem=1 boot
stalls before the root mount completes: no ring flush, no BSD root,
frozen early console text. modem=0 boots fine, and the only delta is
the modem thread.

topaz_soc_map() polls sweet_ufs_read_part("modem_a") in an EAGAIN loop
from the moment the modem thread starts. The poll is meant to wait
until "sweet_ufs comes up with the root device", but a read that lands
while sweet_ufs is still probing can wedge the driver on this unit,
so the root mount never finishes. (The poll's sleeps already happen
under the soc_map once-lock, so waiting there is nothing new.)

Gate the poll on the root vnode: root mounted means sweet_ufs is
fully up, which is exactly what the poll waits for. vfs_rootvnode()
is what this file's original (0113) wait loop used. With root up,
behaviour below is unchanged; if root never appears the poll still
runs after the timeout, as before.

---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazModem.cpp
@@ -630,6 +630,28 @@ topaz_soc_map(void)
 	state = -1;
 	soc_lock = IOLockAlloc();
 	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("modem_part", fw_part, sizeof(fw_part));
+	/* usability fix (xxlloydzz + Ma): on this unit, modem=1 boots wedge
+	 * before the root mount completes. The partition poll below starts
+	 * as soon as the modem thread runs, and a sweet_ufs_read_part()
+	 * that lands while sweet_ufs is still probing can wedge the
+	 * driver, so the root mount never finishes (no ring flush, no
+	 * BSD root). Root mounted means sweet_ufs is fully up -- which is
+	 * what the poll is waiting for -- so gate the poll on the root
+	 * vnode first. With root up, behaviour below is unchanged. */
+	{
+		int i;
+		for (i = 0; i < 300; i++) {
+			vnode_t root = vfs_rootvnode();
+			if (root != NULLVP) {
+				vnode_put(root);
+				break;
+			}
+			IOSleep(1000);
+		}
+		if (i == 300) {
+			LOG("soc_map: root vnode never appeared; polling anyway");
+		}
+	}
 	uint8_t probe[16];
 	int err = EAGAIN;
 	for (int i = 0; i < 120 && err == EAGAIN; i++) {
